IMPORT prelude

-- Economic Development Board Act 1961 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for an enterprise that deals with the Board: what counts
-- as an "enterprise" (s 2, s 22), which of the Board's powers over enterprises need the Minister's written approval and when it may
-- guarantee an enterprise's loan (s 18(2)), the Board's rights on a default (s 19), when it may call in a loan, advance or incentive
-- early (s 20), the High Court enforcement procedure, its appeal period and the stay on release orders (s 21(1), (7), (11), (13)),
-- the Board's immunity for erroneous public information (s 14(3)), protection of staff pension scheme moneys from creditors
-- (s 11(2)(a), (b)), and the two offences: misusing the Board's name or symbol (s 27A) and breach of secrecy (s 27B).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1/4/2022), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/EDBA1961.txt. The cover says the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including
-- 1 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in the body is Act 25 of 2021, with effect from 01/04/2022 (s 21(12)).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0169 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. Most of the Act constitutes the Board; the parts a business meets are the lending and incentive provisions
-- (ss 18-22) and the two offences, so this row is SCOPED to those. Not encoded: establishment and constitution of the Board (ss 3-5,
-- the Schedule), its functions (s 6), ministerial directions, the chief executive and staff (ss 7-9), committees and delegation
-- (s 12), finance, borrowing and shares (ss 16-17A), compulsory acquisition (s 23), land registration (s 26), the seal (s 27),
-- winding up (s 28), regulations (s 29), the rest of s 11(2) (bankruptcy, trusts and nominations), s 14(1), (2), s 19(2)-(4) and the
-- interim-order mechanics of s 21(2)-(6), (8)-(10), (12).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Economic Development Board Act 1961 -- enterprises`

§§ `2 and 22 -- what is an enterprise`

-- s 2: "enterprise" means "any entity incorporated, formed or established in Singapore or elsewhere, whether or not for profit, and
-- howsoever owned or controlled, and includes -- (a) a corporation, a sole proprietorship, a partnership, a joint venture, a trust
-- and an association; and (b) a branch of an enterprise".
-- s 22: references to an enterprise in ss 19, 20 and 21 include "a tourist enterprise as defined in the Tourist Promotion Board Act
-- (Cap. 328, 1985 Revised Edition) in force immediately before 20 November 1997". (That definition was not deposited, so it is not
-- modelled.)
-- That an individual acting in a private capacity, with no entity, is not an enterprise is an INFERENCE from "any entity".
DECLARE Body IS ONE OF
    `a Singapore company`
    `a sole proprietorship`
    `a partnership`
    `a trust`
    `the Singapore branch of an overseas company`
    `a not-for-profit association`
    `a private individual with no business entity`

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is an enterprise` IF
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `a private individual with no business entity` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `18(2) -- powers over enterprises`

-- s 18(2): the Board's powers include "(a) with the written approval of the Minister, to underwrite the issue of stocks, shares, bonds
-- or debentures by enterprises; (b) with the written approval of the Minister, to guarantee ... loans raised by enterprises which --
-- (i) are repayable within a period not exceeding 25 years; or (ii) are floated in the public market; (c) to grant loans or advances
-- to, or subscribe to stocks, shares, bonds or debentures of enterprises; (d) to manage, control or supervise enterprises by nominating
-- directors or advisers ...; (e) with the written approval of the Minister, to establish, sell shares of, invest in and manage
-- enterprises; ... (i) to provide technical advice and assistance to enterprises ...; (n) with the written approval of the Minister,
-- to award compensation to any person sustaining any damage by reason of the exercise of any of the powers under this Act".
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `underwriting an enterprise's share issue`
    `guaranteeing an enterprise's loan`
    `lending to an enterprise`
    `nominating a director to an enterprise`
    `establishing or investing in an enterprise`
    `awarding compensation for damage caused by the Board`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power needs the Minister's written approval` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `lending to an enterprise` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `nominating a director to an enterprise` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `has the Minister's written approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `years to repay` IS A NUMBER, `floated in the public market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may guarantee the loan` IF
        `has the Minister's written approval`
    AND (    `years to repay` AT MOST 25
         OR  `floated in the public market`)

§§ `19 -- rights on default`

-- s 19(1): where an enterprise "which is under a liability to the Board under an agreement makes any default in repayment or
-- otherwise fails to comply with the terms of its agreement", the Board has, "without affecting any other rights or remedies", "the
-- right to take over the management of the enterprise, as well as the right to sell and realise the property pledged, mortgaged,
-- hypothecated or assigned to the Board". No court order is mentioned in s 19 (contrast s 21).
GIVEN `liable to the Board under an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN, `defaulted in repayment` IS A BOOLEAN, `otherwise breached the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may take over management and sell the security` IF
        `liable to the Board under an agreement`
    AND (    `defaulted in repayment`
         OR  `otherwise breached the agreement`)

§§ `20 -- calling for repayment before the agreed period`

-- s 20: "Despite any agreement to the contrary", the Board "may by notice require any enterprise, to which it has granted any loan,
-- advance or incentive, to immediately discharge in full its liabilities" -- "(a) if it appears to the Board that false or
-- misleading information in any material particular was given in the application ...; (b) if the enterprise has failed to comply with
-- the terms of its contract ...; (c) if there is a reasonable apprehension that the enterprise is unable to pay its debts or that
-- proceedings for liquidation may be commenced ...; (d) if the property ... assigned to the Board as security ... is not insured and
-- kept insured ... to the satisfaction of the Board, or depreciates in value, in the opinion of the Board, by more than 20% and
-- further security to the satisfaction of the Board is not given; (e) if, without the permission of the Board, machinery and other
-- equipment ... is removed from the premises of the enterprise without being replaced; or (f) if for any reason it is necessary in
-- the opinion of the Board to protect the interests of the Board."
-- READING: "and further security ... is not given" is read as qualifying only the depreciation limb, so an uninsured security is a
-- ground even if further security is offered. The text can also be read the other way.
DECLARE Grant HAS
    `the Board granted a loan, advance or incentive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `false or misleading material information in the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `breach of the contract terms` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable apprehension of inability to pay or liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `security not kept insured` IS A BOOLEAN
    `percentage depreciation of the security` IS A NUMBER
    `further security given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `machinery removed without permission and not replaced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Board thinks it necessary to protect its interests` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the grant` IS A Grant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may call for immediate repayment` IF
        `the grant`'s `the Board granted a loan, advance or incentive`
    AND (    `the grant`'s `false or misleading material information in the application`
         OR  `the grant`'s `breach of the contract terms`
         OR  `the grant`'s `reasonable apprehension of inability to pay or liquidation`
         OR  `the grant`'s `security not kept insured`
         OR  (    `the grant`'s `percentage depreciation of the security` GREATER THAN 20
              AND (NOT `the grant`'s `further security given`))
         OR  `the grant`'s `machinery removed without permission and not replaced`
         OR  `the grant`'s `the Board thinks it necessary to protect its interests`)

§§ `21 -- enforcement through the High Court`

-- s 21(1): where "by reason of the breach of any condition of an agreement ... the Board becomes entitled to call for the immediate
-- payment of any loan, advance or incentive ... before the due date or where the due date has expired, and the enterprise fails to
-- repay", "any officer of the Board generally or specially authorised by the Board in that behalf may apply to the General Division of
-- the High Court" for sale of the security, transfer of management to the Board, or an interim injunction against removal of
-- machinery.
GIVEN `entitled by a breach to call for early payment` IS A BOOLEAN, `the due date has expired` IS A BOOLEAN, `the enterprise has repaid` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer is authorised by the Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an officer may apply to the High Court under section 21` IF
        (    `entitled by a breach to call for early payment`
         OR  `the due date has expired`)
    AND (NOT `the enterprise has repaid`)
    AND `the officer is authorised by the Board`

-- s 21(7): "If no cause is shown on or before the date specified in the notice ..., the Judge is to immediately make the interim order
-- final". (9): after investigating where cause is shown, the Judge makes an order confirming, varying or releasing the attachment,
-- confirming or dissolving the injunction, or transferring management or rejecting the claim. (10): further orders when releasing.
-- (13): "Any party aggrieved by an order made under subsection (9) or (10) may appeal against the order within 30 days after the date
-- of the order." Subsection (13) names only orders under (9) and (10); a default order under (7) is outside it. Whether some other
-- route of appeal exists was not examined, so this rule says only what s 21(13) gives.
DECLARE Order IS ONE OF
    `a default order under subsection (7)`
    `an order after investigation under subsection (9)`
    `a further order under subsection (10)`

GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order, `days after the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 21(13) allows the appeal` IF
        `days after the order` AT MOST 30
    AND CONSIDER `the order`
        WHEN `a default order under subsection (7)` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 21(11): "Unless the Board intimates to the Judge that it will not appeal against any order releasing any property from attachment,
-- the order is not to be given effect to until the expiry of the period mentioned in subsection (13) ..., or if an appeal is lodged,
-- unless the court hearing the appeal otherwise directs, until the appeal is disposed of."
GIVEN `the Board said it will not appeal` IS A BOOLEAN, `days since the release order` IS A NUMBER, `the Board lodged an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN, `the appeal is disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN, `the appeal court directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the release order can be given effect` IF
    IF `the Board said it will not appeal` THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `the Board lodged an appeal` THEN `the appeal is disposed of` OR `the appeal court directs otherwise`
         ELSE `days since the release order` GREATER THAN 30

§§ `14(3) -- information supplied to the public`

-- s 14(3): where the Board supplies information to the public "pursuant to any written law", neither the Board nor its members,
-- officers or employees "shall be liable for any loss or damage suffered by any member of the public by reason of any error or omission
-- ... if made in good faith and in the ordinary course of the discharge of the duties".
GIVEN `supplied under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN, `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the ordinary course of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 14(3) shields the Board from the error` IF
    `supplied under a written law` AND `in good faith` AND `in the ordinary course of duties`

§§ `11(2)(a), (b) -- pension scheme moneys and creditors`

-- s 11(2)(a), (b): payments and contributions under a Board pension or provident scheme are not "assignable or transferable, or liable
-- to be garnished, attached, sequestered or levied upon for or in respect of any debt or claim whatsoever other than a debt due to the
-- Board or to the Government".
DECLARE Creditor IS ONE OF
    `the Board`
    `the Government`
    `a bank`

GIVEN `the creditor` IS A Creditor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the creditor may garnish scheme moneys` IF
    CONSIDER `the creditor`
    WHEN `a bank` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `27A -- the Board's name and symbol`

-- s 27A(2): "Any person who uses a name, symbol or representation identical with that of the Board, or which so resembles the Board's
-- name, symbol or representation as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or cause confusion, shall be guilty of an
-- offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to
-- both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $250 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- offence continues after conviction." (s 3(3): the Board may act under the business name "EDB".)
GIVEN `uses an identical name or symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `resemblance likely to deceive or confuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is an offence under section 27A` IF
    `uses an identical name or symbol` OR `resemblance likely to deceive or confuse`

GIVEN `days or part days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 27A` MEANS
    10000 PLUS 250 TIMES `days or part days continuing after conviction`

§§ `27B -- preservation of secrecy`

-- s 27B(1): a person who "is or has been" a member, officer, employee or agent of the Board, or a member of a committee, "must not
-- disclose any information relating to the affairs of the Board or of any other person" obtained in their duties "unless the
-- disclosure is made -- (c) with the permission of the person from whom the information was obtained ...; (d) for the purpose of the
-- administration or enforcement of this Act; (e) in compliance with the requirement of any court or as required or allowed under ...
-- any written law; (f) with the prior authorisation from the Board ...; or (g) for the purpose of assisting any public officer or
-- officer of any other statutory board in the investigation or prosecution of any offence". (2): they must not "for his or her own
-- personal benefit or for the personal benefit of any other person, make use of any information" so obtained -- no exceptions are
-- listed. (4): a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both.
DECLARE Basis IS ONE OF
    `no lawful basis`
    `the permission of the person it came from`
    `administering or enforcing the Act`
    `a court requirement or a written law`
    `the Board's prior authorisation`
    `assisting a criminal investigation`

GIVEN `is or was an insider of the Board` IS A BOOLEAN, `the basis` IS A Basis
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence under section 27B` IF
        `is or was an insider of the Board`
    AND CONSIDER `the basis`
        WHEN `no lawful basis` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `is or was an insider of the Board` IS A BOOLEAN, `used the information for personal benefit` IS A BOOLEAN, `the basis` IS A Basis
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is an offence under section 27B` IF
    `is or was an insider of the Board` AND `used the information for personal benefit`
